{{--
  PredictHQ mark.

  Two bars and a step up. It reads as a chart moving in your favour, which
  is the one thing every visitor already knows how to read, and the step
  doubles as the H of HQ once you have seen it.

  The previous mark was a ring with a gap and a centre dot, meant as a
  probability arc. Nobody read it that way. At nav size the gap closed
  optically and it became a circle with a dot, which says nothing, and an
  abstract mark that needs its own caption is not a mark.

  Squared ends and equal stroke weights so it holds at 18px in the nav and
  still looks deliberate at 52px. currentColor throughout, so one file
  serves the light nav, the dark nav, and the footer.
--}}
<svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="width:100%;height:100%;display:block">
  {{-- Baseline bar, held short so the rise reads as a change rather than a pair. --}}
  <rect x="5" y="18" width="6" height="9" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.55" />
  {{-- The step up. Full opacity: this is the subject. --}}
  <rect x="13" y="11" width="6" height="16" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor" />
  <rect x="21" y="5" width="6" height="22" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor" />
</svg>
